    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Route purchase requests from Slack to approval and create POs in NetSuite with Claude\n\nFinance and operations teams that approve purchases in email threads and lose track of them.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: A purchase-request form (or a Slack slash command) starts the workflow; email requests to procurement@ are parsed the same way.\n1. Receive the request\n2. Normalise and complete\n3. Check budget and policy\n4. Route approvals\n5. Create the PO\n6. Send to the supplier\n7. Track receipt\n8. Report committed spend\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus NetSuite / Dynamics / Xero, Slack.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nSet the approval thresholds and the approver map in the Config node; swap NetSuite for Dynamics or Xero.\nGuardrail to keep: No PO is created without the approvals the policy matrix requires; the workflow enforces, it does not decide.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/purchase-order-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}